    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1023">

                <pb facs="0772" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/37.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Brazilian Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>320. Your November 11, No. 203. Department of the opinion that, relative to
                    claims presented by its instructions to Mexican Government, its statement that
                    claimants are American citizens should be accepted as prima facie correct,
                    subject to rebutting evidence by Mexican authorities,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
